odology can  be applied to improve operational  efficiencies and demonstrate the true  value of the lab let's go back to the  concept of total cost of ownership and  there is no better person to speak about  this topic than Patrick Gunn tart  Patrick King can you tell me a little  bit about the benefits of focusing on  TCO and the laboratories you manage and  the clients you work with yes of course  as we heard earlier healthcare leaders  expect the laboratory be more involved  in improving patient management and  reducing the time to diagnosis an  intervention all while dealing with a  complex equation of competing priorities  cutting costs on one side while  increasing performance on the other side  a laboratorian must have previously  focused on cutting costs to help  positively impact his or her  organization's finances but my initial  question to clients is always the same  how are you currently assessing indirect  lab costs and their impact on the  broader healthcare organization many  labs don't know how to start this type  of analysis and that's when we come in  and assist them  you see healthcare organizations are  constantly looking for ways to cut costs  primarily due to the high upfront cost  of the analytic instruments  and the cost of the test themselves as a  result the lab often becomes a target  for downsizing or pure outsourcing I  completely agree with that Patrick and  that's why TCO is an incredibly  important part of TVO cost is part of  the overall value equation whether we  like it or not  so Patrick you are mainly focused on  helping laboratorians understand the  total cost of certain investments or  processes and helping them make  decisions that will minimize these costs  while maximizing operational  efficiencies you recently completed a  study that assesses the TCO of the newly  launched analytical system from Abbott  the illinit ECI series can you tell us  more about it  sure the reason I was interested in  doing this assessment was my 